h Rebel  MPS over house building targets now  there's a clash with backbenches over  onshore wind though this is an amendment  put down by the former leveling up  secretary under Liz trust Simon Clark  and look at some of the names on it they  want to reverse the ban Liz truss and  Boris Johnson amongst the signatures so  what Mr shaps has said on Sky News Today  signaling a U-turn is that where  communities are in favor of it well  sounds as though they can go ahead  where onshore wind happens it needs to  happen with local consent uh what is  being proposed uh is something which  would guarantee that local incentives to  say I haven't studied all the  ramifications uh of that in terms of the  planning changes we need and I'll be  talking about this more later in the  week I've just talked spoken to you  about measures to reduce energy use we  also need to make sure that we reduce  more energy and we'll be doing that  well Rishi sunak made his views clear on  this during the summer Leadership  campaign uh when he put out a press  release saying plans to relax onshore  Wind Farm ban in England to be scrapped  uh he said he'd promise plans to to  scrap plants to relax the ban providing  certainty to rural communities he said I  want to reassure communities I would  scrap plans to relax the ban well sounds  as though there is a u-turn on the way  in the face of uh pressure from some of  those big beasts on the Tory back  benches including two the two most  recent former Prime Ministers okay John  we appreciate your update thank you  time for a look at some of today's other  climate stories now and the prince and  princess of Wales were set to fly to  Boston in the U.S later this week for  this year's Earth shot prize awards  ceremony Billy eilish will headline the  environmental Awards with 15 finalists  vying for a million pounds awarded to  each of the five category winners the  shortlist for the competition which is  in its second year includes london-based  notple